# Result: 06-report (telemetry-benchmark)

test_command=sh tests/bench-harness_test.sh
id=report-01 result=green reason=test_report_01_groups_and_shapes (bench_report_metrics is the pinned closed 11-metric set transcribed from the scenario; the Background JSONL (five dryrun records -- wall 100,200,300,400,1000; tokens_input 1000..5000; cost 0.01,0.02,null,0.04,0.05; outcomes approved x3/error/timeout; model_pinned null,null,m-one,m-one,m-two -- plus one stub record wall 500) is reported through "sh bench/antz-bench.sh report --jsonl <f>" and the report groups by client with "records=" counts, distinct model_pinned values (models=m-one,m-two -- nulls never named), the outcome distribution (outcomes: approved=3 error=1 timeout=1), one line per pinned metric carrying exactly the six statistics n/mean/median/min/max/p95; the all-null tokens_reasoning and tokens_cache_write print "n=0 mean=null median=null min=null max=null p95=null" with a forbidden-zero scan over the group; a hand-written line missing ten metric keys reports them as "absent" with exit 0 and correct stats for the one present; the total record count across groups prints)
id=report-02 result=green reason=test_report_02_pinned_values (exact lines over the Background file: wall_clock_ms n=5 mean=400 median=300 min=100 max=1000 p95=1000; tokens_input n=5 mean=3000 median=3000 min=1000 max=5000 p95=5000; cost_usd n=4 (null excluded) mean=0.03 median=0.03 min=0.01 max=0.05 p95=0.05; stub group wall_clock_ms n=1 mean=500 median=500 min=500 max=500 p95=500; two runs on the same file cmp byte-identical; and a 20-record file 1..20 pins the definitions apart from wrong-but-similar rules -- p95=19 is the ceil(0.95*n)-th sorted value NOT the max, median=10.5 is the standard even-n mean of the two middle values)
id=report-03 result=green reason=test_report_03_baseline_deltas (with --baseline naming a second conforming JSONL whose dryrun wall mean is 150: "wall_clock_ms: current mean=400 median=300 baseline mean=150 median=150 delta=+250" and the negative "client_duration_ms: ... delta=-30" print baseline mean and median beside the current ones with the signed mean delta; cost_usd (values only in the results) prints "absent in baseline" and tokens_reasoning (values only in the baseline) "absent in results" with scans that no "absent" line carries delta= and no delta=0/delta=null is ever invented; one-sided clients print "client stub: absent in baseline (no comparison)" / "client zed: absent in results (no comparison)"; the baseline file is cmp'd byte-identical and still 3 records after the report)
id=report-04 result=green reason=test_report_04_standalone_any_input (on a host whose HOME carries both client config dirs and whose PATH carries a tripwired claude stub, report mode exits 0 on a foreign-mix input (client=claude antz_version=9.9.9 repetition=7, client=opencode version 1.2.3 repetition 3, a hand-written legacy line) against a baseline from a third mix: all three groups aggregate, absent metrics are reported not fatal, the baseline's own clients appear as absent-in-results gaps; the tripwire marker is never created (no client, no adapter), bench/results never exists in the staged checkout (no fixture materialized, no repetition ran), stderr is empty (writes only its report), and both input files cmp byte-identical afterward)

Notes:
- The seam is unchanged: bench_report <results.jsonl> [<baseline.jsonl>] in
  bench/lib.sh, now the full pinned computation (05-runner's wiring and its
  runner-04/06 expectations -- "report" on stdout, client groups, empty
  stdout on refused runs -- still pass). New sibling helper
  bench_report_metrics pins the report's closed metric set (the 06-report
  invariant), mirroring bench_schema_fields.
- Number format: %.6f rounded then trailing zeros/point trimmed (canonical
  minimal decimal like bench_num_add, with rounding that lands IEEE
  summation artifacts back on the exact value: cost mean 0.03). p95 rank is
  integer arithmetic int((95*n+99)/100), never floating ceil.
- Record lines are scanned field-by-field with anchored "key": patterns --
  the shape bench_emit_record writes (compact, pinned key order); flat
  records make this sufficient (documented in the lib comment).
- Suite cost: bench suite 48 -> 52 tests, ~21s -> ~23s; full
  tests/run_all.sh measured 55s (18/18 green) this session at the load seen
  -- the 05-runner receipt's 63s-under-load caveat stands, nothing added
  beyond the four scenario tests.
